# The kinds of agent crew knows, one line a kind. Fields are split by
# spaces, and - is none:
#
#   kind      the name crew records for a member of this kind (kind/<name>)
#   process   the command's name, as ps shows it and a spawn line runs it
#   env       a variable the agent sets for the commands it runs, which
#             tells it apart where a sandbox hides ps
#   idle      the mark that starts its input line, near the bottom of its
#             screen, once it is up and waits for a line
#   approve   the key that answers yes to its command prompt in the gate
#   color     its panes' color, #rrggbb
#   resume    the arguments that resume conversation %s, to the end of the line
#
# The owner's ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/crew/kinds, then a crew's own
# kinds, add kinds or replace these, a line for a kind replacing the one
# before it. The versions each kind was seen with are in
# test/fixtures/VERSIONS.
#
# kind    process  env              idle  approve  color    resume
claude    claude   CLAUDECODE       ❯     enter    #d97757  --resume %s
codex     codex    CODEX_THREAD_ID  ›     y        #10a37f  resume %s
agy       agy      -                >     -        #4285f4  --conversation %s
